diff --git i/docs/usage.md w/docs/usage.md
index 8a51eaf..aea9507 100644
--- i/docs/usage.md
+++ w/docs/usage.md
@@ -23,3 +23,31 @@ lefthook dump
 ```bash
 LEFTHOOK=0 git commit
 ```
+
+## Recovering unstaged changes
+
+Before pre-commit jobs hide partially staged changes, Lefthook saves worktree-specific
+patches under the common Git info directory and creates a stash-shaped backup under
+`refs/lefthook/backup/<commit>`. Shared refs keep linked-worktree backups alive during
+garbage collection from any worktree. Only the current run's ref is removed, with
+compare-and-delete, after successful restoration. Existing and legacy stashes remain
+untouched. Concurrent runs within the same worktree are unsupported.
+
+If restoration fails, patches are missing, or a run stops before cleanup, its backup
+ref remains. These backups do not appear in `git stash list`:
+
+```sh
+git for-each-ref --format='%(refname) %(subject)' refs/lefthook/backup/
+git stash show --patch <ref>
+```
+
+Preserve current edits first. In a clean worktree at the original base, recover both
+the index and working tree, verify the result, then remove only that backup:
+
+```sh
+git stash apply --index <ref>
+git update-ref -d <ref> <commit>
+```
+
+Here `<ref>` is the full recovery ref and `<commit>` is its saved commit ID. Retained
+refs do not expire automatically and may be included in `git push --mirror`.
